{%- comment -%}
  One metal swatch dot.

  **The paint comes from the option value's own swatch and from nowhere else.**
  In admin the Metal option is connected to Shopify's Color metafield, so each
  value carries its own swatch — measured on this shop, Yellow Gold and White
  Gold both resolve to a swatch image, while Gold Karat and Wrist Length
  correctly carry none.

  Nothing here is hardcoded, deliberately. An earlier version matched the value
  text against a table of eight metals and painted from bundled gradients and
  `metal-*.webp` assets. That is exactly the wrong shape: it duplicated data the
  merchant already maintains, went stale the moment a metal was added or
  renamed, and quietly painted the wrong colour for anything it failed to
  recognise. Adding a metal is admin work now, not a theme change.

  A value with no swatch configured paints nothing. The dot keeps its hairline
  and its accessible name, so the metal stays pickable and announced — a
  missing swatch beats an invented one.

  Accepts:
    option_value - the product_option_value drop. The only source.
    size         - pixel width to request for a swatch image. Default 120,
                   which covers the card's 20px dot and the product page's
                   larger one at high density.
    selected     - true when this is the chosen metal. Only used where the dot
                   stands alone; inside a card the wrapping link carries the
                   state instead.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign swatch_paint = blank
  assign swatch = option_value.swatch

  if swatch.color != blank
    assign swatch_paint = swatch.color
  elsif swatch.image != blank
    assign swatch_width = size | default: 120
    assign swatch_url = swatch.image | image_url: width: swatch_width
    assign swatch_paint = swatch_url | prepend: "url('" | append: "')"
  endif
-%}

<span
  class="swatch-dot{% if selected %} is-selected{% endif %}"
  {%- if swatch_paint != blank %} style="--metal-swatch: {{ swatch_paint }};"{% endif -%}
></span>
